                        "review": "Its mediocre at best. Immortal redneck actually looks and runs pretty well. Even the mechanics feel polished however the core gameplay loop is deeply unsatisfying.\n\nUpgrades outside the run are not exciting and the ones in the run range from underwhelming to frustrating. Most of the upgrades you get have a caveat or a negative effect attached to it that you cant see before picking.\n\nEnemies dont drop health drops enough.\n\nThis makes progressing in runs feel almost chore like. You never really feel all that much stronger. \n\nAnother fatal flaw the game has is the sound design and enemy hitreg. While the actual damage registers it feels really weak since the guns sound like childrens toys. It feels like i hit the enemies with a whiffle bat rather than a gun and the enemies further make this worse since they dont give much feedback on dying. Shooting a small enemy with a shotgun doesnt blast them across the floor but makes them play their standard death animation.\n\nThis makes you the player feel weak.\n\nConsidering the game does 3 major things incorrectly - \n1. Sound Design (for guns and enemy imapct)\n2. Kill impact \n3. Poor Buffs during runs\n\nI actually think the game isnt worth playing. You will probably pick it up play it for 1-2 hours think yeah that was cool and then put it aside. \n\nTake the positive reviews of this game with a caveat. Most people dont have a high playtime on the game for a reason.",
